# Gemini: Here is a standard, copy-pasteable block for your .gitignore file:
# Why this matters: * Secrets: If you ever set up database connections, you will likely store your passwords in a .env file. Pushing that file to GitHub, even for a minute, is a major security risk.
# Data Files: Git is designed for text (code), not massive binary files or gigabytes of .csv and .parquet files. Tracking large data files will bloat your repository and make pulling/pushing incredibly slow.

# Environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Python Cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# IDEs and Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Secrets and Configurations (CRITICAL)
.env
config.ini
secrets.json

# Data and Databases
*.csv
*.excel
*.parquet
*.db
*.sqlite3